refutation.attempts:
I read the producer (validators_l0.ml:3374-3455) and `find_verbatim_comment_ranges` (validators_common.ml:2462). meaning.json holds 1 case with 0 hunks. I replicated the rule regex across every .tex file in the corpus (all 2961 packages) and found 5 live papers, which is all there are, so I could not reach 15 real trigger files. I also grepped .bbl/.bib/.cls/.sty/.bst files, but the audit harness edits only *.tex, so those are out of scope. For example, `ceurart.cls` and `cas-common.sty` have `\url{ #1 }` inside macro definitions; that is harmless INFERRED because url.sty ignores spaces anyway.

I built all 5 corpus papers pristine vs fixed and saw no change. Then I built 11 synthetic edge cases:
- verbatim-like contexts: `\verb`, `\lstinline`, fancyvrb Verbatim/BVerbatim, `verbatim*`, alltt, lstlisting;
- url.sty obeyspaces;
- `\url` redefined as `\texttt`;
- a trailing backslash-space inside `\url`, plain and inside `\footnote`.

For each case I did a pristine vs fixed compile, a pdftotext word diff and an `LP_FIX_TRACE` of the source edits. Five verbatim-like contexts showed displayed code being changed.

Recommended verdict: UNSAFE for the allow-list, or safe only after the guard also covers `verbatim*`, `\verb`, `\lstinline`, `\mintinline`, fancyvrb (Verbatim/BVerbatim/LVerbatim) and alltt.
